  "cut": false,
  "source": "# The way down\n\nKydux's own art, made for the game and under the GNU GPL, version 3 or\nlater, like the rest of it.\n\n- Laid out on the grid by `tools/art/layout.py`, painted by Gemini 3 Pro Image\n  (`gemini-3-pro-image`) from `tools/art/prompts/scene-way-down.md` on that\n  layout, then edited by it without its grid and with the arch at the top\n  dimmed (`game-way-down-nogrid.md`).\n- What lies round the corridors painted by Gemini from\n  `game-way-down-voids.md`, joined by `tools/art/repaint.py`.\n- What it still left navy laid with its own stones (`navy`, `tiled`), no model\n  asked.\n- The door opened by `tools/art/door.py` from the painting itself, no model asked.\n- Its key is the storeroom's, cut there; its hole is the storeroom's hole picture\n  from Gemini, laid across the corridor by `tools/art/repaint.py placed`.\n",
  "voids": {
    "about": "What lies round the corridors and rooms, flat and dark as the model left it, painted as the castle's solid stone and dim rooms (D136): by Gemini 3 Pro Image from tools/art/prompts/game-way-down-voids.md on the canvas this makes, shown flat in a dim colour, and joined by tools/art/repaint.py, the painting kept pixel for pixel elsewhere.",
